UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore": true, "boat": true, "ramp": "Public ramps around the harbour are mapped by Transport for NSW; the Sydney Harbour boating map also shows moorings, marinas and wharves", "parking": "Varies by ramp — trailer parking is limited at the popular inner-harbour ramps, especially at weekends", "notes": "IMPORTANT HEALTH ADVICE: NSW Government dietary advice is that no fish or crustaceans caught west of the Sydney Harbour Bridge should be eaten, and catches taken east of the bridge should be limited to 150 g per month. This follows elevated dioxin levels traced to contaminated sediments near Homebush Bay. Commercial fishing and prawn trawling have been banned harbour-wide since 2006. Recreational fishing itself is not banned and catch-and-release is unaffected — multilingual warning signs are posted around the foreshore. Land-based fishing is excellent from the many wharves, rock walls and foreshore reserves.", "sourceUrl": "https://www.dpi.nsw.gov.au/dpi/fishing/recreational-fishing/responsible-fishing/fishing-safely/fishing-in-sydney-harbour"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'sydney-harbour-kingfish';
